WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.220
- We love to spotlight
amazing dads on this show.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.430
And our next dad is a Halloween hero.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:10.277
This is GDP, Good Dad Program.

00:00:10.277 --> 00:00:13.829
(audience cheers)

00:00:13.829 --> 00:00:16.980
Okay, this story comes out of Cincinnati,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.770
where one brave dad engineered

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.680
a trick or treat solution
for the COVID age.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.950
And here to tell us all about it,

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.776
please welcome Andrew Beattie.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:28.338
(audience cheers)

00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:29.704
- Hi Drew, how are you?
- Hi Andrew.

00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:31.117
- Thanks for having me on the show.

00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.800
- Oh, I was gonna say
the same thing to you.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.330
Thank you so much for coming on.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.100
Now, your story is getting
picked up everywhere.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.890
So we're really lucky that you came

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.260
and will talk to us about it, and we-

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.740
- I feel like I'm the lucky
one, but thank you so much.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.490
- Oh thank you Andrew.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.940
Andrew, Drew, cool.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.500
Anyway, I always do that with an Andrew,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.740
and I love it 'cause my
name's like a boy's name

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.750
but I just get excited when I hear it.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.840
So it's no surprise that the CDC

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.080
is like officially called
off trick or treating,

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.320
and they've called it
a high-risk activity.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.410
But you have found a
way to lower the risks.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.660
So will you tell us about it?

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.593
- Absolutely, I'd be happy to.

00:01:12.593 --> 00:01:15.260
So my wife and I, we have a
six year old daughter at home,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.710
and we really love doing creative things,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.690
activities that we can do
together that are fun and safe.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.370
And you know this year,
and really any year,

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.950
practicing safety guidelines

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.130
when trick or treating
is really important.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.940
But especially with COVID-19 this year,

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.690
it was more important
than ever to give people

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.760
an opportunity to maintain those

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.290
social distancing guidelines

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.700
and have some fun with it along the way.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.160
And this was something that we thought

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.760
would be a really great way to do so.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.500
So we used a six foot by
four inch shipping tube

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.600
that we had laying around.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.470
We had played with
dropping some toys down.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.420
And my wife and daughter
and I painted it up orange,

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.640
put some black duct tape
around it and lit it up

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.850
and put it on our rail
to give it a test run.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.160
And it just seemed to
really work really well.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.680
- And people are freaking out about it.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.480
And what I love is that you got something

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.650
so convenient and attainable.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:05.200
This is not a Rube Goldberg contraption

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.670
that people cannot build.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.940
It's like, this is doable for people.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.050
And I have to say that I as a parent,

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.740
I feel sort of rattled when my kids ask me

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.460
how is Halloween gonna function this year?

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.610
Are we gonna get candy?

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.990
Are we gonna go trick or treating?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:23.070
And I know for each sort
of area within our country

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.850
there are different sets of guidelines

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.350
and we're always trying

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:29.220
to overcompensate for our kids anyway.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.960
And I think you've come up with something

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.830
that feels really safe
and doable for parents.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.980
And you really put the
spirit back in Halloween

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.760
and made it a little less difficult

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.260
for us parents to navigate.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.170
- Thank you so much.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.620
You know, we really wanted to do something

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.870
that could allow everyone to participate,

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.860
even those with mobility challenges.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:49.800
This is something that we've been

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.460
talking about doing for years.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.380
You know, you have those
moms with strollers,

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.870
or your people in
wheelchairs that have to stop

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.050
and think about how they can participate

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.170
the same way other people do

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.870
without having to stop and think about it.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.770
And that seems really unfair
to me with something like this.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.940
So this is something that doesn't just

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.540
scratch that one inch, it's something that

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.100
really I think helps a lot of people

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.650
regardless of whether or not
we're dealing with a pandemic.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:13.221
So thank you.

00:03:13.221 --> 00:03:14.054
(audience cheers)

00:03:14.054 --> 00:03:17.330
- I have to say, Andrew,
I think you're bringing

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.860
all the goodness to the name Drew today.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.500
I'm honored that I get that moniker too,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.170
because you really are bringing

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.200
the positivity and the functionality here

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.470
for my favorite holiday of
the year, by the way too!

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.130
Halloween, you don't have to travel,

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.270
you don't have family baggage.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.240
You don't have to get a gift.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.930
It's just the best, I love Halloween!

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:40.580
So thank you, Andrew.
- That's right.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.549
- Thank you.

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:42.382
- You're welcome, my pleasure.

00:03:42.382 --> 00:03:45.241
- Okay everybody, thank you so much.

00:03:45.241 --> 00:03:47.824
(upbeat music)

